Yes.  this has been my default assumption also.  Without it being
probabilistic, you have problems with tenses, numbers of entities, and
so on.  Think of the speakers of Lojban as computers in which the
default values of their programs are fuzzy logic, probabilistic
expressions rather than as single valued expressions.  Of course, this
desktop machine I am typing on would have a hard time with this sort
of expression, but the light weight parallel processor I'm carrying
around on the top of my neck does OK with this sort of default.

